From: glebn2 <40612835+glebn2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] LightsService: send plain black to turn a light off

LineageOS puts the LED brightness into the alpha channel and forces alpha
0 to 0xFF, so turning a light off reaches the HAL as 0xff000000. The
Kyocera lights blob of BALMUDA Phone treats any non-zero alpha as an
active request: a cleared notification (priority 2) kept masking the
charging light (priority 4) until reboot. Apply the brightness alpha only
to a non-black color.
---
 .../core/java/com/android/server/lights/LightsService.java    | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/lights/LightsService.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/lights/LightsService.java
index 08215af..64d0aa0 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/lights/LightsService.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/lights/LightsService.java
@@ -788,7 +788,9 @@ public class LightsService extends SystemService {
             try {
                 if (mVintfLights != null) {
                     HwLightState lightState = new HwLightState();
-                    if (mBrightnessLevel > 0 && mBrightnessLevel <= 0xFF) {
+                    // BALMUDA Phone: the Kyocera blob takes black with alpha for a light-on request
+                    if (mBrightnessLevel > 0 && mBrightnessLevel <= 0xFF
+                            && (color & 0x00FFFFFF) != 0) {
                         int colorAlpha = color >>> 24;
                         if (colorAlpha == 0x00) {
                             colorAlpha = 0xFF;
